      "writtenOn": "2022-04-20T13:59:32Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I discussed with Keith what be the best approach to define an usb muxes chain in the DTS in comments to the bug https://b.corp.google.com/issues/227757117\nWe decided that `usb-muxes` property in usbc node will be good to enforce the order of muxes in chain, since order of children in `*_FOREACH_CHILD` macro is not guaranteed.\n\nI thought about putting usb muxes as a child of the usbc node, but it doesn\u0027t work out because of chain of dependencies in a DTS (discussed here https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromiumos/platform/ec/+/3575157/2..4/zephyr/projects/corsola/usbc_krabby.dts#b36)\n\nPutting usb muxes in port0-mux@0 may be possible option, but it create problem with devices like Intel JHL8040R which is a retimer, but it is also usb mux. If we will relay on that the parent reg property is port number, than JHL8040R would have two nodes: one on I2C bus and second in port0-mux@0. If it is okay to have two nodes in DTS for one device than it is not a problem.\n\nUnfortunately we don\u0027t have doc describing usb muxes configuration yet.",
      "parentUuid": "340e2cf1_29f76bce",
      "revId": "a5405fca324ed9efd3be868cb56319a1112a1fa1",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
