      "writtenOn": "2022-04-21T04:28:33Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "So I think that _FOREACH_CHILD order is guaranteed (and we have code that does rely on that), but it is DT_FOREACH_STATUS_OKAY where the order is not guaranteed.\nSee https://docs.zephyrproject.org/3.0.0/reference/devicetree/api.html?highlight\u003ddt_foreach_status_okay#c.DT_FOREACH_STATUS_OKAY\n\nI haven\u0027t found anywhere where it is stated that _FOREACH_CHILD is not iterated in node order (the documentation for DT_FOREACH_CHILD implies the ordering in the example, as compared to DT_FOREACH_STATUS_OKAY documentation which explicitly states the ordering is not guaranteed, and the example shows that).\n\nIt would be good to get a definitive answer on the ordering, because I think if the child ordering is guaranteed, it\u0027s a much better design to use these mux nodes as children on the port node, and then you don\u0027t have to use a phandle array, and the DTS is more natural.",
      "parentUuid": "fb8c227d_0dd11697",
      "revId": "a5405fca324ed9efd3be868cb56319a1112a1fa1",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
